It is Wednesday morning.
I leave my flat.
I meet my neighbour on the stairs.
"Good morning, Frau Krüger," I say.
"Good morning, Frau Flores," she answers.
Frau Krüger smiles.
"Do you have time today?" she asks.
"Shall we drink a coffee together?"
I always like drinking coffee.
"Yes, I would love to," I say.
"At what time?" I ask.
"Perhaps at six o'clock?" answers Frau Krüger.
I immediately say yes.
But then I think about my calendar.
Oh no, I have an appointment today!
My haircut appointment is also at six o'clock.
That is a problem.
But I want to drink the coffee with Frau Krüger.
"Six o'clock is perfect," I say to her.
I will call the hair salon later.
